# Log Console Copy & Export Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Turn the daemon log screen into a usable diagnostic console — copy to clipboard, export to a file, search, level filter, and a pause that no longer discards lines.

**Architecture:** All console state moves out of the view into `LogConsoleModel` (`@MainActor @Observable`) in ReachyUI, mirroring the existing `MovesModel` + `MovesModelTests` pattern. The model owns the ring buffer, level parsing, the filtered `visible` cache and the export payload; `LogConsoleScreen` renders it and owns only presentation state (scroll position, buffer-size preference). Export goes through a `Transferable` value that serializes lazily, so building it on every toolbar render is cheap.

**Tech Stack:** Swift 6 (strict concurrency), SwiftUI, Observation, CoreTransferable, UniformTypeIdentifiers, swift-testing.

**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-03-log-console-copy-export-design.md`

## Global Constraints

- Swift 6 strict concurrency. `LogConsoleModel` is `@MainActor`; `LogEntry` / `LogExport` are `Sendable` value types.
- API floor is macOS 14 / iOS 17: do NOT use `ScrollPosition`, `onScrollPhaseChange` or `onScrollGeometryChange` (all iOS 18+). Scroll tracking uses a sentinel row with `onAppear`/`onDisappear`.
- Never call tools bare. Build `./bin/mise run build`, test `./bin/mise run test`, filter `./bin/mise run test:filter ReachyUITests`, lint `./bin/mise run lint`, format `./bin/mise run format`.
- ReachyUI never talks to the network directly except through ReachyKit clients; `LogStreamClient` stays the only transport here.
- `#if os(iOS)` only for platform-exclusive APIs (the pasteboard). No per-platform view copies.
- No redundant comments. Comment only non-obvious "why", one terse line.
- Tests use swift-testing (`@Suite` / `@Test` / `#expect`), not XCTest.
- Conventional commits (enforced by the commit-msg hook).

---

